  "interpretation": "Moving trust from input space to reflex signatures makes label-poisoned candidates visible in this synthetic task. The result also reproduces the weak-pool problem: valid novel reflexes can be rejected until the trusted pool is expanded. Parameter-subspace membership alone is not sufficient, because an adaptive candidate can be generated inside the parameter subspace while harming a target slice. Behavior-space residuals catch that constructed parameter-space attack here, but the signature-only control shows that behavior-space geometry is not a semantic certificate either."
